    <GaugingStation location="Torrington" name="Torridge" number="50002">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station built in 1960 and reconstructed in 1977.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Station reconstructed in 1977. Mobile bed. Low profile structure installed 2006 to mimic and stabilise natural bed control. Overtopping begins on left bank at about 3.3m. Well calibrated throughout range. Multiple ratings applied across period of record. Ratings since 1977 have identical top limbs. Well calibrated throughout range. No major changes to catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station on straight reach built in 1960. Main channel 28m wide, cableway span 57m.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Records prior to Oct 1962 unreliable.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Moderate modification to flows from Meldon Reservoir. Runoff also affected by abstraction for public water supply and industry/agriculture and effluent returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Large, rural catchment draining coastal hills in the west and Dartmoor Granite in the south. Geology mostly Carboniferous shales and sandstones of the Culm. Moorland, rough grazing and generally low grade agricultural land.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">SRPEI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged beyond AMAX3. Rating confirmed by gaugings both in and out of bank." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
